      "label": "Cat is mapped as a Jew",
      "description": "The text 'you're a cat, not a jew' explicitly maps the visual entity 'cat' onto the textual entity 'Jew', using the cat as a stand-in for Jewish people in an antisemitic stereotype. This is a direct analogical mapping where the visual subject (cat) is equated with a targeted group (Jews) through the text.",
